{"chunk_id":"R2-2111630-001","collection":"ran2_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":[],"tdocNumber":"R2-2111630","title":"Delegates work overload and organizational enhancements"},"point_id":"5309049884946993827"}
This document is a report of the discussion by email on the RAN2 reflector on “Delegates work overload”, labelled in the subject by [AT116-e][000] Delegates Work overload. In chronological order Based on the comments given as above + Chair additional comments (below). Chair: Many companies agree that delegate’s load is an issue. However it is not easy to identify WG level operational enhancements that would have significant impact on delegates load. The suggestion to increase pre-filtering was met both with criticism and support. Introduction of formal feature lead positions was briefly discussed, and was met with significant scepticism (argumentation similar to earlier discussion in RAN2). Chair: There were many smaller suggestions applicable to the WG that should be considered by R2 leadership, e.g. Ensure that there is no overlap between long email discussions and summaries, no overlap between long email discussions and submitted tdocs etc (may impact tdoc limitations), be careful in allocating new long email discussions, Ensure that offline discussions (at-meeting and between meetings) focus on what can be taken into account, e.g. by limiting the number of proposals to be discussed, or having other limit etc. Chair: Some proposals, e.g. that long email discussions deadline shall be well in advance of tdoc deadline for a meeting, can be considered but for many meetings may not be realistic as inactive periods has reduced the time possible for long email discussions. Chair: There was recognition that preparation efforts, summaries, offline discussions etc is important for good utilization of GTW time. Chair: There were also a number of proposals on the table that are plenary scope rather than WG scope, e.g. one meeting per Q, removal of functionality from WIs. Chair: a number of companies commented that the coincidence of TSG RAN R18 preparation discussion and RAN2 meeting preparation was not good and should be avoided future-wise.

{"chunk_id":"R2-2111630-006","collection":"ran2_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":[],"tdocNumber":"R2-2111630","title":"Delegates work overload and organizational enhancements"},"point_id":"16962788422918943059"}
s a long email discussion for a WI/SI If there is a "long" email discussion for a certain Work Item, that means that several of the open issues for that Work Item will be sorted out within the long email discussion. Given this, we think the Tdoc cap can be reduced by 1 for each "long" email discussion for a Work Item. There may, in special cases be some company who want to provide input on the topic discussed in the "long" email discussion. This should not be the normal case, but it may happen. Hence we don’t see that the minus 1 Tdoc has to mean that companies are not allowed to have Tdocs on the topic covered by the email discussion. But a general rule of reducing the Tdoc cap by one for each "long" email discussion for a Work Item will help us at least a bit in reducing the overload situation in RAN2.

